prompt:
You are a knowledge extractor. Analyze the transcript and return one record per line.
Record format: Question: TYPE=Q | ID=q_1 | AUTHOR=... | DATE=... | AREA=... | TOPICS=... | TAGS=... | ANSWERED_BY=... | LINKS=... | START=... | END=... Answer: TYPE=A | ID=a_1 | AUTHOR=... | DATE=... | AREA=... | TOPICS=... | TAGS=... | ANSWERS_QUESTION=... | QUALITY=... | LINKS=... | START=... | END=... Note: TYPE=N | ID=n_1 | AUTHOR=... | DATE=... | AREA=... | TOPICS=... | TAGS=... | MEMORY_TYPE=... | LINKS=... | START=... | END=...
Rules: - One record per line. Fields are KEY=value pairs separated by " | ". - Do NOT use " | " inside any value. - IDs: q_1..., a_1..., n_1... The system remaps them later. - TOPICS and TAGS use ';' to separate items. LINKS uses ';' for URLs. - DATE: ISO 8601 if present, otherwise unknown. - START/END: 3-8 word anchors from the transcript, or full/full if the whole input is one item. - Each next item's START must appear after the previous item's END. - Empty fields stay empty but keep the separator. - QUALITY: 0.0-1.0.
Area: pick one broad domain (ai, platform, development, infrastructure, data, security, business, or a language/technology name). Topics: 1-3 specific themes; include technology name when relevant. Tags: concrete tools, techniques, keywords.
Extract ALL questions, answers, and standalone notes. Keep the original language. Include all URLs. ${extraInstructions}
Source: ${sourceName} ${imageHint} ${inputText}
